{{define "content"}}
<section class="st-hero">
  <div class="container st-hero-inner">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Northlight Studio</p>
      <h1>We shape brands that people remember</h1>
      <p class="lead">A small design studio with a big list of projects. We build identities, packaging, web sites and printed matter for companies that care about the details.</p>
      <div class="row"><a class="btn" href="#work">See our work</a><a class="btn secondary" href="#pricing">Prices</a></div>
    </div>
    <img src="/images/gallery-04.svg" alt="Abstract pattern in blue and violet" width="1200" height="800">
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container st-section" aria-labelledby="clients">
  <h2 id="clients" class="visually-hidden">Clients</h2>
  <ul class="logos">
    <li>Aldersey Bank</li><li>Marren Foods</li><li>Tidewater Press</li><li>Lumen Optics</li><li>Pinewood Cycles</li><li>Orchard &amp; Co</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="container st-section" aria-labelledby="services">
  <h2 id="services">What we do</h2>
  <p class="muted">Six services, one team, and a fixed price for every package.</p>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card"><h3>Brand identity</h3><p>A name, a logo, a color system and the rules of use. We deliver a guide that a new hire can follow on the first day.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Web design</h3><p>Pages that load fast and read well on a phone. We design in the browser, so the result is the page that you ship.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Packaging</h3><p>Boxes, labels and sleeves. We test each design on the shelf of a real shop before it goes to print.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Print</h3><p>Reports, magazines and posters. We prepare the files for the printer and check the first proof with you.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Motion</h3><p>Short animations for a product, a talk or a social post. Every clip comes with a version without sound.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Research</h3><p>Interviews and tests with the people who use your product. We report what we saw, not what we hoped to see.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="st-dark" aria-labelledby="work">
  <div class="container st-section">
    <h2 id="work">Selected work</h2>
    <div class="portfolio">
      <figure><img src="/images/gallery-02.jpg" alt="Hills at dusk, a poster for a hiking festival" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1067"><figcaption>Poster, Aldersey Hiking Festival</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/images/gallery-05.jpg" alt="Morning mist over green hills, a tea label" loading="lazy" width="1280" height="853"><figcaption>Label, Marren Tea</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/images/gallery-03.png" alt="Colored circles on a gradient, a book cover" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="800"><figcaption>Cover, Tidewater Press</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/images/gallery-14.jpg" alt="Warm desert dunes, a campaign photo" loading="lazy" width="1800" height="1200"><figcaption>Campaign, Lumen Optics</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/images/gallery-13.svg" alt="Overlapping shapes, a pattern for a bicycle shop" loading="lazy" width="1800" height="1200"><figcaption>Pattern, Pinewood Cycles</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/images/gallery-09.jpg" alt="A night sky above a quiet valley" loading="lazy" width="960" height="640"><figcaption>Annual report, Orchard &amp; Co</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container st-section" aria-labelledby="process">
  <h2 id="process">How a project runs</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><h3>Listen</h3><p>We spend a week with your team. We read what you wrote and we ask what you did not write.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Sketch</h3><p>Three directions on paper. You pick one, and we drop the others without regret.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Build</h3><p>We make the real thing in weekly steps. Every Friday you see a working version.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Hand over</h3><p>Files, guides and a call with the people who will use them. We stay on the phone for thirty days.</p></li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="st-tint" aria-labelledby="voices">
  <div class="container st-section">
    <h2 id="voices">What clients say</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <blockquote><p>They changed our tea box and our sales moved in a month. The shop owners now ask for the new label by name.</p><footer>Rina Alder, Marren Foods</footer></blockquote>
      <blockquote><p>The report finally reads like a story. Our auditors sent a thank-you note, which has never happened before.</p><footer>Tomas Wick, Orchard &amp; Co</footer></blockquote>
      <blockquote><p>We asked for a logo and we got a system. It still works on a bike frame and on a tiny app icon.</p><footer>Hana Pell, Pinewood Cycles</footer></blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container st-section" aria-labelledby="pricing">
  <h2 id="pricing">Prices</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <caption>Fixed price packages in euros, without tax</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Package</th><th scope="col">Includes</th><th scope="col" class="num">Weeks</th><th scope="col" class="num">Price</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Spark</th><td>Name check, logo, two colors, one page of rules</td><td class="num">3</td><td class="num">4,800</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Flame</th><td>Spark, a web site of five pages, business cards, a social kit</td><td class="num">8</td><td class="num">14,500</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Beacon</th><td>Flame, packaging for three products, a printed guide, a launch film</td><td class="num">16</td><td class="num">38,000</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Lighthouse</th><td>Beacon, research with 30 users, a year of support</td><td class="num">26</td><td class="num">72,000</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container st-section" aria-labelledby="faq">
  <h2 id="faq">Questions</h2>
  <details><summary>Do you work with small companies?</summary><p>Yes. Half of our clients have fewer than ten people. The Spark package exists for them.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Who owns the files?</summary><p>You do. We hand over every source file with the final invoice, and the licenses of the fonts that we bought for you.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Can we change the plan during the project?</summary><p>You can. We agree on the change and on its price in writing before we start on it.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Where is the studio?</summary><p>In an old rope factory by the harbour. Visitors are welcome on Thursdays, and there is always coffee.</p></details>
</section>

<section class="st-cta">
  <div class="container st-section">
    <h2>Tell us what you want to make</h2>
    <p>We answer every message within two working days.</p>
    <form class="search-form" action="/search" method="get"><label class="visually-hidden" for="cta-mail">Your email</label><input id="cta-mail" name="mail" type="email" placeholder="you@example.com"><button type="button">Start a project</button></form>
  </div>
</section>
{{end}}
